-- Bulk-load lifetime invoice + payment history from Skydo payment records
-- (PaymentDetailFile_23.09.2026 (1).xlsx + INVOICE_5793_23.09.2026 (1).zip).
-- 164 distinct invoices, 167 payment rows (3 invoices were
-- each paid in two installments and get one invoice row + two payment rows).
-- All rows are already-settled/paid invoices, recorded directly as paid (not
-- going through the app's draft->paid transition) since this is a historical
-- backfill, not new billing activity.
--
-- Idempotent by design (safe to re-run):
--   1. Insert any invoice row that doesn't already exist for that
--      (client_id, invoice_number) pair.
--   2. Flip any pre-existing-but-not-yet-paid invoice (e.g. one entered by
--      hand before this bulk load) to paid with the correct paid_at/
--      conversion_rate.
--   3. Insert a payment row for any (invoice, amount, date) combination that
--      doesn't already exist — matched this way, rather than "does this
--      invoice have any payment at all", so a split-payment invoice can get
--      both of its installments inserted without the first blocking the
--      second.
--
-- Per explicit instruction: no founder-payout recompute is triggered by this
-- script (recomputeFounderPayoutForMonth only runs from the app layer) —
-- historical /founders figures are intentionally left untouched.

